  "family": "electronic",
  "lineage": "Club music from Ottawa, where the DJ collective A Tribe Called Red, formed in 2007 and later renamed The Halluci Nation, ran Electric Pow Wow nights that mixed recordings of powwow drum groups with hip hop, moombahton and dubstep beats. This powwow-step sound set drum-group songs over bass-heavy electronic production; the group's records appeared on Tribal Spirit and Radicalized Records, and it won the 2014 Juno Award for Breakthrough Group of the Year. The powwow-drum and voice cards stand for the sampled drum-group recordings.",
